            <h4>US Pre-Clearance at DUB</h4>
            <p>Dublin is one of the few airports outside North America offering US customs and immigration pre-clearance.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Complete US immigration and customs inspection before departure</li>
                <li>Arrive in Boston as a domestic passenger with no immigration queues</li>
                <li>Saves significant time upon arrival at Logan, particularly during peak morning bank</li>
                <li>Available to all passengers on eligible flights regardless of cabin class</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Immigration and Customs at DUB</h4>
            <p>Passengers arriving from Boston proceed through Irish entry controls.</p>
            <p><b>Requirements:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Valid passport with at least six months' validity beyond planned departure</li>
                <li>Electronic Travel Authorization (ETIAS) for US citizens (once fully implemented)</li>
                <li>Proof of accommodation for border inspection</li>
                <li>Return or onward travel documentation</li>
                <li>US citizens enjoy visa-free access for tourism stays up to 90 days</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Transportation from DUB to Central Dublin</h4>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Aircoach and Airlink - </b>Express bus services to city center hotels and key points; cost approximately €7-€10; journey time 25-40 minutes</li>
                <li><b>Dublin Bus - </b>Routes 16 and 41 provide economical service to the city center; cost approximately €3.30; journey time 40-60 minutes</li>
                <li><b>Taxi / Uber / Free Now - </b>Typical fares to central Dublin €25-€35; journey time 20-30 minutes depending on traffic</li>
                <li><b>Car Rental - </b>Major agencies located in both terminals; useful for exploring Ireland beyond Dublin</li>
            </ul>
